I couldn't add `clever otoroshi open swaggerui` because all my file writes were blocked. I haven't changed anything, so nothing has been run or validated. If you allow writes to the repo, I'll apply the changes below, then run `npm run docs` and `npm run validate`.

**What I found:** the Otoroshi details from `Operator.getDetails()` already include `api.swaggerUrl`, and `clever otoroshi get` prints it as "Swagger URL". The new command only needs to open that URL in the browser, the same way `open webui` opens `accessUrl`.

**Planned changes:**

1. **`src/lib/operator-commands.js`**: add a helper next to `operatorOpenWebUi`. It throws an error you can act on if the add-on has no Swagger URL.
   ```js
   export async function operatorOpenSwaggerUi(provider, addonIdOrName) {
     const operator = await Operator.getDetails(provider, addonIdOrName);
     const swaggerUrl = operator.api?.swaggerUrl;
     if (swaggerUrl == null) {
       throw new Error(`No Swagger UI available for ${styleText('red', operator.addonId)}`);
     }
     await openBrowser(swaggerUrl, `Opening ${styleText('blue', operator.addonId)} Swagger UI in the browser…`);
   }
   ```
2. **New `src/commands/otoroshi/otoroshi.open.swaggerui.command.js`**: a copy of `otoroshi.open.webui.command.js` that calls `operatorOpenSwaggerUi('otoroshi', addonIdOrName)`. It uses `since: null`, as new commands must.
3. **`src/commands/global.commands.js`**: import it and register `swaggerui: otoroshiOpenSwaggeruiCommand` under `otoroshi.open`, between `logs` and `webui`.
4. **`docs/operators.md`**: add a `clever otoroshi open swaggerui myOtoroshi` example after the `open logs` / `open webui` examples.

`skills/clever-tools/SKILL.md` doesn't mention the Otoroshi open commands, so it needs no change. The command reference (`otoroshi.docs.md`) is generated by `npm run docs`, which calls the public Clever Cloud API and so needs network access.

